eh-MAK"],["to translate","tərcümə etmək","tahr-jew-MA et-MAK"],["to graduate","bitirmək","bee-teer-MAK"]]}],"grammar":[{"id":"pronouns","title":"Pronouns","text":["Azerbaijani often drops the pronoun, because the verb ending shows who is speaking. There is no he / she difference: \"o\" means both."],"rows":[["I","mən","man"],["you (informal)","sən","san"],["he / she / it","o","o"],["we","biz","beez"],["you (formal or plural)","siz","seez"],["they","onlar","on-LAR"]],"ex":[["I am a student","mən tələbəyəm","man tah-lah-bah-YAM"],["you are tall","sən hündürsən","san hewn-dewr-SAN"],["she is my older sister","o mənim böyük bacımdır","o mah-NEEM buh-YEWK bah-juhm-DUHR"],["we are friends","biz dostuq","beez dos-TOOG"],["they are teachers","onlar müəllimdirlər","on-LAR mew-ahl-leem-deer-LAR"]]},{"id":"singular-and-plural","title":"Singular and plural","text":["Add -lar or -lər, by vowel harmony. After a number, the noun stays singular: iki kitab (two book)."],"rows":[["kitab (book)","kitablar","kee-tab-LAR"],["ev (house)","evlər","ev-LAR"],["uşaq (child)","uşaqlar","oo-shag-LAR"],["after a number: singular","iki kitab","ee-KEE kee-TAB"]],"ex":[["one house, houses","bir ev, evlər","beer EV ev-LAR"],["one book, books","bir kitab, kitablar","beer kee-TAB kee-tab-LAR"],["one cat, cats","bir pişik, pişiklər","beer pee-SHEEK pee-sheek-LAR"],["two books","iki kitab","ee-KEE kee-TAB"],["the children","uşaqlar","oo-shag-LAR"]]},{"id":"to-be-am-san-d-r","title":"To be: -am, -san, -dır","text":["There is no separate verb \"to be\". Add an ending to the noun or adjective. After a vowel, the ending changes: tələbə-yəm (I am a student)."],"rows":[["I am","-am / -əm / -yam / -yəm","am"],["you are","-san / -sən","san"],["he / she is","-dır / -dir / -dur / -dür","duhr"],["we are","-ıq / -ik / -uq / -ük","uhg"],["you are (formal)","-sınız / -siniz","suh-NUHZ"],["they are","-dırlar / -dirlər","duhr-LAR"]],"ex":[["I am a student","mən tələbəyəm","man tah-lah-bah-YAM"],["you are tired","sən yorğunsan","san yor-goon-SAN"],["he is a doctor","o həkimdir","o hah-keem-DEER"],["we are happy","biz xoşbəxtik","beez khosh-bakh-TEEK"],["they are at home","onlar evdədirlər","on-LAR ev-dah-deer-LAR"]]},{"id":"var-and-yox-have-there-is","title":"Var and yox: have, there is","text":["Azerbaijani says \"my X exists\" (var) or \"my X does not exist\" (yox). The ending shows the owner: -ım / -im (my), -ın / -in (your), -ı / -i (his)."],"rows":[["there is","var","var"],["there is not","yox","yokh"],["I have","mənim ... -ım var","var"],["I do not have","mənim ... -ım yoxdur","yokh-DOOR"]],"ex":[["I have an older brother","mənim böyük qardaşım var","mah-NEEM buh-YEWK gar-dah-SHUHM var"],["I have a car","mənim maşınım var","mah-NEEM mah-shuh-NUHM var"],["I do not have time","vaxtım yoxdur","vahkh-TUHM yokh-DOOR"],["there is a problem","problem var","prob-LEM var"],["there is no water","su yoxdur","soo yokh-DOOR"]]},{"id":"present-tense-r","title":"Present tense: -ır","text":["Verb stem + -ır / -ir / -ur / -ür + person ending. Gəlmək (to come): gəl-ir-əm."],"rows":[["I come","gəlirəm","geh-lee-RAM"],["you come","gəlirsən","geh-leer-SAN"],["he / she comes","gəlir","geh-LEER"],["we come","gəlirik","geh-lee-REEK"],["you come (formal)","gəlirsiniz","geh-leer-see-NEEZ"],["they come","gəlirlər","geh-leer-LAR"]],"ex":[["I am eating bread","mən çörək yeyirəm","man chuh-RAK yeh-yee-RAM"],["you are reading a book","sən kitab oxuyursan","san kee-TAB o-khoo-yoor-SAN"],["she works in a bank","o bankda işləyir","o bank-DAH eesh-lah-YEER"],["we drink tea","biz çay içirik","beez chay ee-chee-REEK"],["they are sleeping","onlar yatırlar","on-LAR yah-tuhr-LAR"]]},{"id":"basic-sentences","title":"Basic sentences","text":["The verb goes last. Order: who, where or when, what, verb. Azerbaijani has no articles: \"kitab\" means \"a book\" or \"the book\"."],"rows":[["I read a book","mən kitab oxuyuram","man kee-TAB o-khoo-yoo-RAM"],["she drinks tea","o çay içir","o chay ee-CHEER"],["we go to school","biz məktəbə gedirik","beez mak-tah-BA geh-dee-REEK"]],"ex":[["I read a book","mən kitab oxuyuram","man kee-TAB o-khoo-yoo-RAM"],["he drinks tea","o çay içir","o chay ee-CHEER"],["we go to school","biz məktəbə gedirik","beez mak-tah-BA geh-dee-REEK"],["they eat bread","onlar çörək yeyirlər","on-LAR chuh-RAK yeh-yeer-LAR"],["the teacher writes","müəllim yazır","mew-ahl-LEEM yah-ZUHR"]]},{"id":"negation","title":"Negation","text":["Put -mı / -mi / -mu / -mü after the verb stem: gedirəm (I go), getmirəm (I do not go). For nouns use \"deyil\" (is not). \"Yox\" means \"there is not\". Always compare with the positive form."],"rows":[["I go","gedirəm","geh-dee-RAM"],["I do not go","getmirəm","get-mee-RAM"],["is","-dır","duhr"],["is not","deyil","deh-YEEL"]],"ex":[["I want","mən istəyirəm","man is-tah-yee-RAM"],["I do not want","mən istəmirəm","man is-tah-mee-RAM"],["I speak English","mən ingiliscə danışıram","man een-gee-lees-JA dah-nuh-shuh-RAM"],["I do not speak English","mən ingiliscə danışmıram","man een-gee-lees-JA dah-nuhsh-muh-RAM"],["I like it","xoşuma gəlir","kho-shoo-MAH geh-LEER"],["I do not like it","xoşuma gəlmir","kho-shoo-MAH gel-MEER"],["she is here","o buradadır","o boo-rah-dah-DUHR"],["she is not here","o burada deyil","o boo-rah-DAH deh-YEEL"],["I have a car","mənim maşınım var","mah-NEEM mah-shuh-NUHM var"],["I do not have a car","mənim maşınım yoxdur","mah-NEEM mah-shuh-NUHM yokh-DOOR"],["I understand","başa düşürəm","bah-SHAH dew-shew-RAM"],["I do not understand","başa düşmürəm","bah-SHAH dewsh-mew-RAM"],["we are tired","biz yorğunuq","beez yor-goo-NOOG"],["we are not tired","biz yorğun deyilik","beez yor-GOON deh-yee-LEEK"],["he works on Sundays","o bazar günləri işləyir","o bah-ZAR gewn-lah-REE eesh-lah-YEER"],["he does not work on Sundays","o bazar günləri işləmir","o bah-ZAR gewn-lah-REE eesh-lah-MEER"]]},{"id":"asking-questions","title":"Asking questions","text":["Add the little word -mı / -mi / -mu / -mü after the word you are asking about. It is the same for every question."],"rows":[["you are a student","sən tələbəsən","san tah-lah-bah-SAN"],["are you a student?","sən tələbəsənmi?","san tah-lah-bah-san-MEE"],["he is here","o buradadır","o boo-rah-dah-DUHR"],["is he here?","o buradadırmı?","o boo-rah-dah-duhr-MUH"]],"ex":[["is this your book?","bu sənin kitabındır?","boo sah-NEEN kee-tah-buhn-DUHR"],["are they here?","onlar buradadırlarmı?","on-LAR boo-rah-dah-duhr-lar-MUH"],["do you like tea?","çayı xoşlayırsan?","chah-YUH khosh-lah-yuhr-SAN"],["is it cold?","soyuqdurmu?","so-yoog-door-MOO"],["do you speak English?","ingiliscə danışırsanmı?","een-gee-lees-JA dah-nuh-shuhr-san-MUH"]]},{"id":"question-words","title":"Question words","text":["Question words stand where the answer would stand."],"rows":[["what","nə","nah"],["who","kim","keem"],["where","harada","hah-rah-DAH"],["when","nə vaxt","nah VAKHT"],["why","niyə","nee-YA"],["how","necə","neh-JA"],["how much","nə qədər","nah gah-DAR"],["which","hansı","hahn-SUH"]],"ex":[["what is your name?","adınız nədir?","ah-duh-NUHZ nah-DEER"],["who is he?","o kimdir?","o keem-DEER"],["where do you live?","harada yaşayırsınız?","hah-rah-DAH yah-shah-yuhr-suh-NUHZ"],["when is the lesson?","dərs nə vaxtdır?","dars nah vahkht-DUHR"],["why are you late?","niyə gecikmisiniz?","nee-YA geh-jeek-mee-see-NEEZ"],["how are you?","necəsiniz?","neh-jah-see-NEEZ"],["how much is it?","nə qədərdir?","nah gah-dahr-DEER"],["which book?","hansı kitab?","hahn-SUH kee-TAB"]]},{"id":"possessives-and-liking","title":"Possessives and liking","text":["Endings go on the noun: -ım / -im (my), -ın / -in (your), -ı / -i (his / her). To say you like something, use \"xoşuma gəlir\" (it comes to my liking)."],"rows":[["my book","kitabım","kee-tah-BUHM"],["your book","kitabın","kee-tah-BUHN"],["his / her book","kitabı","kee-tah-BUH"],["our book","kitabımız","kee-tah-buh-MUHZ"],["your book (formal)","kitabınız","kee-tah-buh-NUHZ"]],"ex":[["my phone","telefonum","teh-leh-fo-NOOM"],["your house (formal)","eviniz","eh-vee-NEEZ"],["his sister","onun bacısı","o-NOON bah-juh-SUH"],["I like music","musiqi xoşuma gəlir","moo-see-GEE kho-shoo-MAH geh-LEER"],["I love football","mən futbolu sevirəm","man foot-bo-LOO seh-vee-RAM"]]},{"id":"formal-vs-informal","title":"Formal vs informal","text":["sən (informal): friends, family, children. siz (formal): strangers, older people, work. Verb endings change: -san / -sən (informal), -sınız / -siniz (formal)."],"rows":[["how are you?","necəsən? / necəsiniz?","neh-jah-SAN / neh-jah-see-NEEZ"],["you speak","danışırsan / danışırsınız","dah-nuh-shuhr-SAN / dah-nuh-shuhr-suh-NUHZ"],["your name","adın / adınız","ah-DUHN / ah-duh-NUHZ"]],"ex":[["how are you? (informal)","necəsən?","neh-jah-SAN"],["how are you? (formal)","necəsiniz?","neh-jah-see-NEEZ"],["where are you going? (informal)","hara gedirsən?","hah-RAH geh-deer-SAN"],["where are you going? (formal)","hara gedirsiniz?","hah-RAH geh-deer-see-NEEZ"],["please sit down (formal)","əyləşin, zəhmət olmasa","ay-lah-SHEEN zah-MAT ol-mah-SAH"]]},{"id":"past-and-future-simple","title":"Past and future (simple)","text":["Past: -dı / -di / -du / -dü + person ending (getdim = I went). Future: -acaq / -əcək + person ending (gedəcəyəm = I will go)."],"rows":[["I went","getdim","get-DEEM"],["you went","getdin","get-DEEN"],["he went","getdi","get-DEE"],["we went","getdik","get-DEEK"]],"ex":[["yesterday I was tired","dünən yorğun idim","dew-NAN yor-GOON ee-DEEM"],["I will study tomorrow","sabah oxuyacağam","sah-BAH o-khoo-yah-jah-GAM"],["we went to the park","biz parka getdik","beez par-KAH get-DEEK"],["I saw him","mən onu gördüm","man o-NOO gur-DEWM"],["she wrote a letter","o məktub yazdı","o mak-TOOB yaz-DUH"]]},{"id":"commands","title":"Commands","text":["Informal: the bare verb stem. Formal: add -ın / -in (gəlin). To forbid, add -ma / -mə after the stem."],"rows":[["come (informal)","gəl","gel"],["come (formal)","gəlin","geh-LEEN"],["do not come","gəlmə","gel-MA"],["sit down","otur","o-TOOR"]],"ex":[["come here","bura gəl","boo-RAH GEL"],["do not come here","bura gəlmə","boo-RAH gel-MA"],["sit down","otur","o-TOOR"],["do not sit down","oturma","o-toor-MAH"],["be quiet","sakit ol","sah-KEET OL"],["do not be late","gecikmə","geh-jeek-MA"],["open the door","qapını aç","gah-puh-NUH ACH"],["close the window","pəncərəni bağla","pan-jah-rah-NEE bahg-LAH"],["listen to me","mənə qulaq as","mah-NA goo-LAHG AS"],["do not worry","narahat olma","nah-rah-HAT ol-MAH"],["speak slowly","yavaş danış","yah-VASH dah-NUHSH"],["wait a moment","bir az gözlə","beer AZ guz-LA"]]},{"id":"can-must-want","title":"Can, must, want","text":["Can: verb + a bilmək (üzə bilirəm, I can swim). Must: \"lazımdır\" or \"gərək\" (needed). Want: istəyirəm (verb + -maq)."],"rows":[["I can swim","üzə bilirəm","ew-ZA bee-lee-RAM"],["I cannot swim","üzə bilmirəm","ew-ZA beel-mee-RAM"],["I must go","getməliyəm","get-mah-lee-YAM"],["I want to go","getmək istəyirəm","get-MAK is-tah-yee-RAM"]],"ex":[["I can swim","mən üzə bilirəm","man ew-ZA bee-lee-RAM"],["I cannot swim","mən üzə bilmirəm","man ew-ZA beel-mee-RAM"],["can you help me?","mənə kömək edə bilərsiniz?","mah-NA kuh-MAK eh-DA bee-lahr-see-NEEZ"],["we must go","biz getməliyik","beez get-mah-lee-YEEK"],["we must not go","biz getməməliyik","beez get-mah-mah-lee-YEEK"],["I want to eat","yemək istəyirəm","yeh-MAK is-tah-yee-RAM"],["I do not want to eat","yemək istəmirəm","yeh-MAK is-tah-mee-RAM"],["you can come","gələ bilərsiniz","geh-LA bee-lahr-see-NEEZ"],["you cannot come","gələ bilməzsiniz","geh-LA beel-maz-see-NEEZ"],["she wants to study","o oxumaq istəyir","o o-khoo-MAG is-tah-YEER"],["I must work today","bu gün işləməliyəm","boo GEWN eesh-lah-mah-lee-YAM"],["you must not run","qaçmaq olmaz","gach-MAG ol-MAZ"]]},{"id":"in-on-at","title":"In, on, at","text":["Azerbaijani uses endings, not words in front: -da / -də (in, on, at), -a / -ə (to), -dan / -dən (from), -ın / -in (of)."],"rows":[["in / on / at","-da / -də","dah / dah"],["to","-a / -ə","ah / ah"],["from","-dan / -dən","dan / dan"],["of","-ın / -in","uhn / een"]],"ex":[["the book is on the table","kitab masanın üstündədir","kee-TAB mah-sah-NUHN ews-tewn-dah-DEER"],["the cat is under the table","pişik masanın altındadır","pee-SHEEK mah-sah-NUHN al-tuhn-dah-DUHR"],["I am at school","mən məktəbdəyəm","man mak-tab-dah-YAM"],["I am at home","mən evdəyəm","man ev-dah-YAM"],["the shop is next to the bank","mağaza bankın yanındadır","mah-gah-ZAH bah-nkuhn yah-nuhn-dah-DUHR"],["the park is near the station","park vağzalın yaxınlığındadır","park vahg-zah-LUHN yah-khuhn-luh-guhn-dah-DUHR"],["we meet in the morning","biz səhər görüşürük","beez sah-HAR gur-rew-shew-REWK"],["the lesson is at nine","dərs saat doqquzdadır","dars sah-AT dok-kooz-dah-DUHR"],["the key is in the bag","açar çantadadır","ah-CHAR chan-tah-dah-DUHR"]]},{"id":"comparing-things","title":"Comparing things","text":["Put \"daha\" before the adjective for \"more\": daha böyük. For \"the most\" put \"ən\" before it: ən böyük. \"Than\" is -dan / -dən."],"rows":[["big, bigger, the biggest","böyük, daha böyük, ən böyük","buh-YEWK dah-HAH buh-YEWK an buh-YEWK"],["small, smaller, the smallest","kiçik, daha kiçik, ən kiçik","kee-CHEEK dah-HAH kee-CHEEK an kee-CHEEK"]],"ex":[["big, bigger, the biggest","böyük, daha böyük, ən böyük","buh-YEWK dah-HAH buh-YEWK an buh-YEWK"],["small, smaller, the smallest","kiçik, daha kiçik, ən kiçik","kee-CHEEK dah-HAH kee-CHEEK an kee-CHEEK"],["this is better than that","bu ondan yaxşıdır","boo on-DAN yakh-shuh-DUHR"],["this is worse than that","bu ondan pisdir","boo on-DAN pees-DEER"],["she is taller than me","o məndən hündürdür","o man-DAN hewn-dewr-DEWR"],["Tashkent is bigger than Samarkand","Daşkənd Səmərqənddən böyükdür","dahsh-KAND sah-mahr-gand-DAN buh-yewk-DEWR"],["it is the cheapest","bu ən ucuzdur","boo an oo-jooz-DOOR"],["the same as","kimi","kee-MEE"]]},{"id":"everyday-sentences","title":"Everyday sentences","text":["Quick sentences to copy and change."],"rows":[],"ex":[["he is a teacher","o müəllimdir","o mew-ahl-leem-DEER"],["you (plural) are students","siz tələbəsiniz","seez tah-lah-bah-see-NEEZ"],["I am happy","mən xoşbəxtəm","man khosh-bakh-TAM"],["she is at school","o məktəbdədir","o mak-tab-dah-DEER"],["you are my friend","sən mənim dostumsan","san mah-NEEM dos-toom-SAN"],["it is cold","soyuqdur","so-yoog-DOOR"],["I study English","mən ingilis dilini öyrənirəm","man een-gee-LEES dee-lee-NEE uy-rah-nee-RAM"],["he teaches maths","o riyaziyyat öyrədir","o ree-yah-zee-YAT uy-rah-DEER"],["they work every day","onlar hər gün işləyirlər","on-LAR har GEWN eesh-lah-yeer-LAR"],["is this your book?","bu sizin kitabınızdır?","boo see-ZEEN kee-tah-buh-nuhz-DUHR"],["are they here?","onlar buradadırlarmı?","on-LAR boo-rah-dah-duhr-lar-MUH"],["do you like tea?","çayı xoşlayırsınız?","chah-YUH khosh-lah-yuhr-suh-NUHZ"],["what time is it?","saat neçədir?","sah-AT neh-chah-DEER"],["whose book is this?","bu kimin kitabıdır?","boo kee-MEEN kee-tah-buh-DUHR"],["how old are you?","neçə yaşınız var?","neh-CHA yah-shuh-NUHZ var"],["how do you say it?","bunu necə deyirsiniz?","boo-NOO neh-JA deh-yeer-see-NEEZ"],["your book (formal)","kitabınız","kee-tah-buh-NUHZ"],["their house","onların evi","on-lah-RUHN eh-VEE"],["my phone","telefonum","teh-leh-fo-NOOM"],["excuse me, sir","bağışlayın, cənab","bah-guhsh-lah-YUHN jah-NAB"],["please sit down (formal)","əyləşin, zəhmət olmasa","ay-lah-SHEEN zah-MAT ol-mah-SAH"],["come here (informal)","bura gəl","boo-RAH GEL"],["yesterday I was tired","dünən yorğun idim","dew-NAN yor-GOON ee-DEEM"],["I will study tomorrow","sabah oxuyacağam","sah-BAH o-khoo-yah-jah-GAM"],["we went to the park","biz parka getdik","beez par-KAH get-DEEK"]]}],"name":"Azerbaijani","id":"az","flag":"az","note":""}